      "heading": "B — Audience, level and prerequisites: passing, backing, parking, intersections and roundabouts",
      "learner_facing": false,
      "markdown": "## B — Audience, level and prerequisites: passing, backing, parking, intersections and roundabouts\nAudience: first-time North Carolina applicants preparing for the regular Class C knowledge test, in English; right of way at intersections [A03] and parking distances [A02] are frequent test topics.\nLevel: scenario application plus exact distances; the parking distances look alike, so contrast drills matter.\nPrerequisites: the speed and lane position section (keeping right, lane changes) and the emergency vehicle rules, which reappear inside roundabouts.\nSensitivity: none beyond legal accuracy; distances and rules are stated as printed.\n",
